.TH WLIST-EXPORT 1 "18 November 2026" "version 0.3.1"
.SH NAME
wlist-export \- export wishlist data.
.SH SYNOPSIS
wlist export [path/to/database]
[--title <title> | -t <title>]
[--css <CSS input> | -c <CSS input>]
[--output-file <file path> | -o <file path>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export Wishlist to file.
.PP
Supported formats include:
.RS
.IP
JSON
.IP
TSV
.IP
HTML
.IP
ODS
.IP
Excel
.RE
.PP
Exports are done based on file extension.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -t <title>, --title <title>
The title of the HTML output
.TP
.B -c <CSS input>, --css <CSS input>
The CSS styling for the HTML output.
.PP
To influence the item list use
.B #registry
.PP
The note list is affected by
.B #notes
.TP
.B -o <file path>, --output-file <file path>
The file to write to.
.PP
This determines the kind of output too.
.SH AUTHOR
Bryce Campbell (tonyhawk2100@gmail.com)
.SH EXAMPLES
Export list to TSV:
.RS
wlist export -o items.tsv
.RE
.PP
Export list to HTML with title:
.RS
wlist export -t "Birthday List" -o wishlist.html
.RE
.PP
Export list with CSS from file:
.RS
wlist export -c style.css -o wishlist.html
.RE
.PP
Export list to HTML with provided CSS:
.RS
echo "body { color: #ff00ff; }" | wlist export -c - -o wishlist.html
.RE